  "reading": "そそぐ",
  "romaji": "sosogu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-godan",
  "gloss": "to wipe out (a disgrace); to avenge; to clear (one's name)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to wipe out (a disgrace); to avenge; to clear (one's name)",
      "explanation": "To remove or make up for a disgrace, dishonor, or humiliating defeat, typically by achieving a later success or victory. A formal, somewhat literary word, most often used with objects such as {恥|はじ} (shame) or {汚名|おめい} (a bad name)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30089_sosogu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{恥|はじ}を{雪|そそ}ぐ。",
      "english": "to wipe out a disgrace.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30089_sosogu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{前回|ぜんかい}の{負|ま}けを{雪|そそ}いだ。",
      "english": "I avenged the previous loss.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30089_sosogu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{汚名|おめい}を{雪|そそ}ぐために、{彼|かれ}はもう{一度|いちど}{挑戦|ちょうせん}することを{決|き}めた。",
      "english": "In order to clear his tarnished name, he decided to take on the challenge once more.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal, literary verb meaning to erase a disgrace by a subsequent achievement.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive; the thing wiped out (a disgrace, defeat, or bad reputation) takes を.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {恥|はじ}を{雪|そそ}ぐ: to wipe out one's shame\n- {汚名|おめい}を{雪|そそ}ぐ: to clear one's tarnished name\n- {雪辱|せつじょく}を{果|は}たす: to achieve one's revenge (the related noun {雪辱|せつじょく} is far more common in everyday speech)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe kanji {雪|そそ}ぐ is also read すすぐ, which more usually means \"to rinse\" (also written {濯|すす}ぐ). In the \"wipe out a disgrace\" sense, the reading そそぐ is standard. Note this word is distinct from {注|そそ}ぐ (to pour), a homophone.",
